1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,043
Every place in your universe so far

2
00:00:03,493 --> 00:00:07,407
is somewhere the crew looks at from the bridge.

3
00:00:09,207 --> 00:00:11,380
This one they fly into.

4
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:15,324
And then one of them gets out.

5
00:00:17,124 --> 00:00:19,733
By the end of this lecture

6
00:00:20,183 --> 00:00:23,226
your universe has a ruin in it,

7
00:00:23,676 --> 00:00:27,154
and a story that runs through its rooms.

8
00:00:28,354 --> 00:00:32,702
Writing a ruin is a whole class of its own.

9
00:00:33,602 --> 00:00:36,646
So today I'm handing you one, finished.

10
00:00:38,446 --> 00:00:42,359
What we're learning is how a universe holds it.

11
00:00:43,259 --> 00:00:47,607
A ruin in a universe never says where it is.

12
00:00:48,057 --> 00:00:49,796
The landmark says that.

13
00:00:51,596 --> 00:00:55,074
It needs one place marked as its entrance.

14
00:00:55,974 --> 00:00:58,148
And it needs two keys.

15
00:00:58,598 --> 00:01:02,076
One on the thing that blocks the way,

16
00:01:02,526 --> 00:01:05,135
and one on the ruin itself.

17
00:01:06,335 --> 00:01:08,509
A new file, called hollow.

18
00:01:09,409 --> 00:01:12,017
I paste the whole ruin in.

19
00:01:13,817 --> 00:01:17,296
Don't read every line, just read its shape.

20
00:01:19,096 --> 00:01:21,270
Three rooms, joined by passages,

21
00:01:21,720 --> 00:01:23,459
and one way in.

22
00:01:24,359 --> 00:01:26,967
A slab, fallen across one doorway.

23
00:01:27,867 --> 00:01:33,085
And behind the slab, a niche with a stone bowl in it.

24
00:01:34,885 --> 00:01:37,059
The bowl is an item,

25
00:01:37,509 --> 00:01:41,422
and it lives in this file with the ruin.

26
00:01:42,622 --> 00:01:45,665
Now the landmark, in the universe file.

27
00:01:46,565 --> 00:01:49,174
It's a landmark like any other,

28
00:01:49,624 --> 00:01:51,363
with two more lines.

29
00:01:53,163 --> 00:01:55,337
Relic, and the ruin's key.

30
00:01:56,237 --> 00:01:59,715
Relic file, and the name of the file.

31
00:02:01,515 --> 00:02:03,254
That's the whole join.

32
00:02:04,154 --> 00:02:06,328
And there's no terrain line,

33
00:02:06,778 --> 00:02:09,822
because a ruin brings its own cloud.

34
00:02:11,022 --> 00:02:12,761
And now the story.

35
00:02:13,661 --> 00:02:16,704
A lead that takes the crew there.

36
00:02:17,604 --> 00:02:21,517
A step that's done when the slab is cut.

37
00:02:22,417 --> 00:02:26,765
And a step that's done when the bowl is taken.

38
00:02:28,565 --> 00:02:30,739
Look at those two signals.

39
00:02:31,639 --> 00:02:33,813
I didn't make them up,

40
00:02:34,263 --> 00:02:37,307
and nothing in my files sends them,

41
00:02:37,757 --> 00:02:39,496
because the game does.

42
00:02:41,296 --> 00:02:46,078
It builds each word from a key in the ruin's file.

43
00:02:46,978 --> 00:02:50,022
Slab, then opened, and hollow, then taken.

44
00:02:51,222 --> 00:02:55,135
I run lint, and all seven files are clean.

45
00:02:56,935 --> 00:02:59,543
Lint looked in the ruin's file.

46
00:03:00,443 --> 00:03:03,052
It found a barrier called slab,

47
00:03:03,502 --> 00:03:06,980
so it knows the game sends slab opened.

48
00:03:08,780 --> 00:03:12,693
Watch what happens if I get the word wrong.

49
00:03:13,593 --> 00:03:17,072
There's one warning, on the step that waits,

50
00:03:17,522 --> 00:03:20,565
and it says nothing sends that word.

51
00:03:21,465 --> 00:03:24,943
So I fix it, and it's clean again.

52
00:03:26,143 --> 00:03:27,883
Let's go in, then.

53
00:03:28,783 --> 00:03:32,261
There's a fourth lead in the quest log,

54
00:03:32,711 --> 00:03:34,450
and I engage it.

55
00:03:35,350 --> 00:03:37,089
The Hollow is charted,

56
00:03:37,539 --> 00:03:39,713
and the next step appears.

57
00:03:41,513 --> 00:03:45,426
I bring the ship up to the way in.

58
00:03:46,326 --> 00:03:50,239
And now a handheld has something new on it.

59
00:03:50,689 --> 00:03:52,428
It says suit up.

60
00:03:53,328 --> 00:03:55,067
So out I go.

61
00:03:55,967 --> 00:03:58,141
The suit knows two places,

62
00:03:58,591 --> 00:04:01,200
the gallery door and the niche.

63
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:06,478
At the door, the slab is a target.

64
00:04:07,378 --> 00:04:10,857
I cut it, and that takes twelve seconds.

65
00:04:11,757 --> 00:04:14,365
The step is done, and paid.

66
00:04:15,265 --> 00:04:17,439
Then on to the niche.

67
00:04:18,339 --> 00:04:20,513
The bowl comes with me,

68
00:04:20,963 --> 00:04:23,137
and that's the last step.

69
00:04:24,337 --> 00:04:28,685
I have to be honest about what you just saw.

70
00:04:29,585 --> 00:04:34,367
When I checked this page, a script flew all of it,

71
00:04:34,817 --> 00:04:37,426
and nobody was watching a screen.

72
00:04:39,226 --> 00:04:42,270
And the exosuit has one known fault.

73
00:04:43,170 --> 00:04:47,952
A console can close the first time it meets one mid-game.

74
00:04:48,852 --> 00:04:51,896
It's reported, and it isn't your file.

75
00:04:52,346 --> 00:04:55,824
The way round it is on the page.

76
00:04:57,024 --> 00:05:01,372
Now the part that makes a ruin fit a campaign.

77
00:05:03,172 --> 00:05:06,215
I go home, and I come back.

78
00:05:07,115 --> 00:05:09,724
The game rebuilt the whole place.

79
00:05:10,174 --> 00:05:12,348
And the slab's still cut.

80
00:05:13,248 --> 00:05:14,987
The bowl's still gone,

81
00:05:15,437 --> 00:05:17,611
and nobody paid me twice.

82
00:05:19,411 --> 00:05:22,454
Now I close the game, and continue,

83
00:05:22,904 --> 00:05:25,078
and it's the same again.

84
00:05:26,878 --> 00:05:29,922
And here it is in the save.

85
00:05:30,372 --> 00:05:34,285
The ruin, what was opened, and what was taken.

86
00:05:35,485 --> 00:05:38,093
One note before you go on.

87
00:05:38,993 --> 00:05:43,776
The battle lectures were written for a universe with no ruin.

88
00:05:44,676 --> 00:05:47,720
So three small things read differently there,

89
00:05:48,170 --> 00:05:50,778
and they're listed on the page.

90
00:05:52,578 --> 00:05:54,317
Now it's your turn.

91
00:05:55,217 --> 00:05:59,565
Give The Hollow your own name and your own words.

92
00:06:00,465 --> 00:06:02,639
Play it to the bowl.

93
00:06:03,089 --> 00:06:07,002
Go home, come back, and look at that slab.
